Remember, it's good practice to have assertions in your production code as well, but you should remove/disable them for production code before deployment. They're helpful for debugging and unit testing, but they can slow down your application.
--------------------Here is the corresponding code with Debug.Assert statements:

```cs
namespace ArrayList.Test
{
    public partial class ArrayListContractTest
    {
        public void PUT_InsertContract([PexAssumeUnderTest]ArrayList arrList, int x, int index)
        {
            AssumePrecondition.IsTrue(index <= arrList.Count && index >= 0);

            int Old_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int Old_x = x;
            int Old_index = index;
            int Old_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
            int Old_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool Old_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            arrList.Insert(index, x);

            int New_arrListCount = arrList.Count;
            int New_arrListIndexOfX = arrList.IndexOf(x);
            int New_arrListLastIndexOfX = arrList.LastIndexOf(x);
            bool New_arrListContainsX = arrList.Contains(x);

            Debug.Assert(index <= Old_arrListCount);
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListCount + 1 == New_arrListCount);
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListIndexOfX == -1 || Old_arrListIndexOfX <= index);
            Debug.Assert(New_arrListIndexOfX >= index);
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListLastIndexOfX == -1 || Old_arrListLastIndexOfX <= index);
            Debug.Assert(New_arrListLastIndexOfX >= index);
            Debug.Assert(Old_arrListContainsX || New_arrListContainsX);
            Debug.Assert(!Old_arrListContainsX || New_arrListContainsX);

        }
    }
}
```

Please note, `Debug.Assert` can be ignored during runtime by the default behavior of the debugger, and it is a way to assert pre- and post-conditions for your code. 

I also made an assumption that the `index` will never be equal to the count of the `arrList` initially. Otherwise, the post-condition `New_arrListCount == Old_arrListCount + 1` would be false.
